From: Ben Bangert <100193+bbangert@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: rockchip: px30: export the I2S1 source clock

The I2S1 fractional divider takes clk_i2s1_src straight from GPLL at
1.2 GHz by default, and at that input it runs the I2S far slower than
programmed: playback on the FRAME156 stalls with write errors. At 600 MHz
it's exact. Give clk_i2s1_src an ID so a device tree can set its rate
with assigned-clocks.

---
--- a/include/dt-bindings/clock/px30-cru.h
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/clock/px30-cru.h
@@ -174,6 +174,7 @@
 #define PCLK_ISP		351
 #define PCLK_CIF		352
 #define PCLK_OTP_PHY		353
+#define SCLK_I2S1_SRC		354
 
 /* pmu-clocks indices */
 
--- a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-px30.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-px30.c
@@ -628,7 +628,7 @@
 	GATE(SCLK_I2S0_RX_OUT, "clk_i2s0_rx_out", "clk_i2s0_rx_out_pre", CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
 			PX30_CLKGATE_CON(10), 11, CLK_GATE_HIWORD_MASK),
 
-	COMPOSITE(0, "clk_i2s1_src", mux_gpll_npll_p, 0,
+	COMPOSITE(SCLK_I2S1_SRC, "clk_i2s1_src", mux_gpll_npll_p, 0,
 			PX30_CLKSEL_CON(30), 8, 1, MFLAGS, 0, 7, DFLAGS,
 			PX30_CLKGATE_CON(10), 0, GFLAGS),
 	COMPOSITE_FRACMUX(0, "clk_i2s1_frac", "clk_i2s1_src", CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
